  "body": "**Risk: HIGH** (analysis hash, persisted form, the Agent's level approval and the PLoT wire). Code verdict: CODEX CEE BUDDY, then the DL's HIGH read. Meaning: AIQ **PASS** at `cae5fac` (5918289470), re-confirmed at `7b5d2c701` (5927366322).\n\n**Why.** A downtime limit on an option with one figure scores exactly 100% or 0%. ISL Talchain/Inference-Service-Layer#216 and PLoT Talchain/plot-lite-service#424 (both on staging) sample and forward a stated range. CEE is the last hop: it must write the range, store it safely, hash it and send it.\n\n**What.**\n1. **Producer.** B6's ask (\"What's each option's likely range for X?\", #2384) has somewhere to land.\n   - `propose_option_interventions` takes `likely_low` / `likely_high` beside a level the user gave.\n   - **Typed admission only (Codex CR 5963331228; 3 Oct):** both ends, 0 < low < high, `range_meaning === 'likely_range'` and `range_user_stated: true`, beside a user-stated level inside the range. No parsing of the user's words. A 95% interval, a min\u2013max or a bound is refused, and the Agent is told to ask.\n   - The approval label says \"likely between 5 days and 20 days (read as the middle half of what's likely)\".\n   - On approval, the range rides the figure through the real door onto the cell as `{low, high, meaning: 'likely_range', source: 'user_specified'}`.\n2. **Hash.** `projectIntervention` reads the published `intervention.fields` (v5: + `range`).\n   - Editing 5\u201320 \u2192 5\u201330 days moves the hash, and so does who stated it.\n   - A graph with no range hashes byte-identically (pinned).\n3. **Writer gate.** At `projectGraphForPersistence`, a range is removed, value untouched, when it is malformed, has no `source`, has a meaning outside the enumerated set, or doesn't contain its value. Refusals are logged as ids and reasons only.\n4. **Wire.** `run_analysis` adds `options[].intervention_ranges[f] = {low, high, meaning}` only where the wire number is the raw point. No range \u2192 no key. The Run's input snapshot records the range as sent, so a range-only edit diffs as `partial`.\n5. **Schemas.** `cee-v3.ts` imports `InterventionRangeSchema` / `InterventionRangeMeaning` from `@talchain/schemas`; the local mirror is gone. **This PR no longer vendors a schemas pack**: staging now vendors 0.69.0 (merged in at `17da9baef`), which carries S1/S2. The PR's rows and the graph-hash suites are green on 0.69.0.\n\n**Tests (RED-first).**\n- `intervention-range.test.ts`: 17 rows.\n- `run-analysis-intervention-range-wire.test.ts`: 5 rows through the real handler, including the snapshot `partial` row and the no-range control.\n- `agent-level-keeps-the-users-likely-range.test.ts`: 21 rows through the real in-process door. That includes AIQ's at-most, asked, comparator and bare-\"and\" rows, all RED before their fixes, plus span-form controls. Mutants: the encoder and \"helper always true\" both turn their rows RED.\n- **3 Oct CR fixes at `e7f365a6`:** a range needs a finite numeric level; a range lost to unit projection withholds that option's limit P; a replacement figure keeps the old range only when the quantity is unchanged; the no-op checks compare the complete range. Required 4/4 green at `e7f365a6`.\n- **Rebased 3 Oct** to one commit on staging `9a9bf022` (head `c168e169`), with the PR's own lines unchanged. Required 4/4, Integration and Typecheck Drift are green at `c168e169`. Schemas are now 0.73.0 from staging, and its `intervention.fields` still includes `range`. The three red advisory checks (Security Audit, Graph Evaluator, Conversation Harness Gates) are red on `staging` too (5916235783).\n\n**Known limits.**\n- `source_quote` isn't recorded; the words are on the turn, not the cell.\n- Only `likely_range` is written; hard-bound wording is not proposed.\n- After merge: one served witness on the 2-month deadline, then STOP.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_019qzyMt4YNwbw753SpzRgW6\n\n",
